{"step_index":182,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-19T15:15:29Z","thinking":"The output indicates an image classification model was trained, mapping an input image to one of five defect categories. This classification model architecture fundamentally lacks the capability to predict bounding box coordinates, because this is outside its defined task. This confirms why the model is only outputting class probabilities, and is not outputting any bounding box data.\n\n\nA simple edge/threshold heuristic failed to reliably identify defect regions, misinterpreting lighting artifacts as defects. The challenge now is to authentically explain the model's defect classifications using evidence the model itself provides. Grad-CAM will visualize the neural network's attention regions, highlighting the areas driving the classification decision.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"python -c \\\"\\nimport torch\\nfrom PIL import Image\\nimport numpy as np\\nfrom ultralytics import YOLO\\n\\nmodel = YOLO(r'D:\\\\acceleration\\\\best.pt')\\nprint('Model layers:', len(list(model.model.modules())))\\n\\n# Test a forward pass and feature extraction\\ndummy = Image.fromarray(np.random.randint(0, 255, (224, 224, 3), dtype=np.uint8))\\nresults = model(dummy, verbose=False)\\nprint('Probs:', results[0].probs.data.cpu().numpy())\\n\\\"\"","Cwd":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\win-10\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\scratch\\\\neurax_app\"","WaitMsBeforeAsync":"5000","toolAction":"\"Testing PyTorch Grad-CAM with YOLO\"","toolSummary":"\"Test model forward pass\""}}]}
