{"step_index":227,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-19T15:18:04Z","content":"### 🎯 Solved with PyTorch Grad-CAM Neural Activation!\n\n---\n\n### 🔍 Why It Was Highlighting the Wrong Area Before\nYour trained YOLOv8 model (`best.pt`) is an **Image Classification Model** (`ClassificationModel` with 5 output classes: `crack`, `hole`, `normal`, `rust`, `scratch`).\n\n- Classification models predict a single category for the **entire image** rather than object detection bounding box coordinates.\n- When we previously used generic computer vision edge/threshold filters on metal surfaces, random lighting glare, shadows, and reflections were mistakenly picked up instead of the real defect.\n\n---\n\n### 🚀 What We Upgraded (PyTorch Grad-CAM Integration)\n\n1. **Exact AI-Driven Defect Localization (Grad-CAM)**:\n   - We hooked directly into YOLOv8’s **final feature layer (`Layer 8: C2f`)** via PyTorch backpropagation.\n   - For every classified defect (`rust`, `scratch`, `crack`, `hole`), the system computes the **Gradient-weighted Class Activation Map (Grad-CAM)**.\n   - The bounding box is now anchored **directly on where the AI neural network's neurons actually fired**, eliminating phantom boxes and lighting artifacts!\n\n2. **New Interactive Overlay Modes in the Grid**:\n   You can now switch live between 3 visualization modes using the radio toggle above the grid:\n   - **🎯 AI Bounding Box**: Crisp bounding box with HUD target brackets centered on the neural network's activation zone.\n   - **🔥 Grad-CAM Heatmap**: Full thermal gradient heatmap (Blue $\\rightarrow$ Green $\\rightarrow$ Red) showing the exact visual evidence YOLO used to make its decision.\n   - **📷 Raw Image**: Original untouched image.\n\n3. **Multi-Column Inspection Grid**:\n   - Inspected units are displayed in a **3-column responsive card grid**.\n   - Includes full **Class Probability Progress Bars** (e.g. `Rust: 94.2%`, `Normal: 4.1%`, `Scratch: 1.7%`) f